  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ε</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> denote the dimensional formula of the permittivity of vacuum. If <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>=</mo></math> mass, <math><mtext>L</mtext><mo>=</mo></math> length, <math><mtext>T</mtext><mo>=</mo></math> time and <math><mtext>A</mtext><mo>=</mo></math> electric current, then dimensions of permittivity is given as <math> <mrow> <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>M</mtext> <mtext>p</mtext> </msup> <msup> <mtext>L</mtext> <mtext>q</mtext> </msup> <msup> <mtext>T</mtext> <mtext>r</mtext> </msup> <msup> <mtext>A</mtext> <mtext>s</mtext> </msup> </mrow> </mfenced></mrow> </math>. Find the value of <math><mfrac><mrow><mtext>p</mtext><mo>-</mo><mtext>q</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>r</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "From Coulomb's law,<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ε</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ε</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>",
